# Errors

Throw an HttpError for an expected client failure. Its status and message become the response. Unexpected errors return a generic 500 without leaking the original message.

```ts
import { Router, HttpError } from "tinyhttp"

const app = new Router()
app.get("/users/:id", request => {
  if (!/^\d+$/.test(request.params.id ?? "")) throw new HttpError(400, "Use a numeric user id")
  return Response.json({ id: request.params.id })
})
```

Supply onError in RouterOptions to integrate your own reporting. Never serialize unknown errors to a public response. Invalid path encoding and malformed query encoding return 400. An oversized JSON body returns 413, and malformed JSON returns 400.

The default response body is `{ "error": "message" }`. The logger records path and status without query strings or body values.
